    "introduction": "Persimmon builds homes in the UK through brands including Persimmon Homes and Charles Church, alongside activity supplying housing partners. It acquires land, secures permissions and constructs residential developments before selling completed homes. The group also manufactures some building components, including timber-frame products, bricks and roof tiles, supporting its construction supply chain. Revenue depends on home completions and selling prices, while profitability reflects land, labour and material costs. Capital is committed ahead of sales, making development timing and customer demand important to cash flow. Mortgage affordability, planning requirements and build quality influence the pace and economics of its projects.",
